> happens to be around).

But a seperate snakestaff item in addition to the above would be very
cool. Almost as cool as sword-chucks, in fact.

UnIDed a snakestaff would look like a normal quarterstaff, and most of
the time it would behave like one. However you could #invoke it to
turn into a snake. Whether it is tame, hostile or just peaceful would
depend on some formula involving the BUC status of the staff.

The #invoked snake would revert back to a snakestaff when it dies, but
it could be a charged item, so you can't just keep #invoking and
#invoking indefinitely. When it's out of charges, it's just a normal
quarterstaff. You can use a scroll of charging but if you try to
overcharge it it should (a) explode (b)turn into a snake corpse (c)
generate a shedload of angry, slithery varmints or (d) all of the
above.

The type of snake it turns into could be determined by the staff's
enchantment (high positive enchantment/ low negative enchantment=big
snake, 0 enchantment=small snake.) By default, the staff would produce
constrictor-type snakes (pythons, boas etc) but if you poison the
staff it produces venomous snakes. Negative enchantments increase the
probability of generating a hostile snake, even on an uncursed or
blessed staff, so watch out for those cursed ?oEW.

It sounds like quite a powerful addition, but like all the best things
in nethack it does come with a few drawbacks: If it's cursed and
negatively enchanted, you'd want to invoke it just to get the damn
thing un-welded from your hands, but then you have to fight the
resulting (big) snake, and for the first round at least, you'll be
barehanded.

Even a blessed snakestaff can put you in an awkward position- you can
unleash this nasty pet on a roomfull of nasties, but to do so you have
to sacrifice your wielded weapon. It makes the idea of keeping a
decent backup weapon a little more meaningful.

All in all it would be a nice little extra toy- especially for
spellcasters who might actually find themselves making a real
weapon-choice once in a while, instead of ditching quarterstaves for
magicbane at the first opportunity.

